invariant: INV-16
file: base64.c
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: base64_class tests its first two ranges with an if chain, so
  whether a key file's character is a capital, a small letter or neither
  decides which path runs, a fact about the scalar's bits. The class is
  the same, so no test sees it; the branch count does, on every spec,
  where base64.c's ceiling is zero (docs/decisions.md 131).

--- old
    uint32_t x = c;
    uint32_t upper = range_mask(x, 'A', 'Z');
--- new
    uint32_t x = c;
    if (x >= 'A' && x <= 'Z') {
        return (uint8_t)(x - 'A');
    }
    if (x >= 'a' && x <= 'z') {
        return (uint8_t)(x - 'a' + 26U);
    }
    uint32_t upper = range_mask(x, 'A', 'Z');
